# models/archives

This module maintains a precomputed year/month index of a blog's published,
visible entries in Redis, so `app/blog/render/retrieve/archives.js` can serve
the `/archives` page without re-fetching and re-grouping every entry on every
request. It mirrors `models/tags`: entries are indexed incrementally as they
are saved, with a full rebuild available for backfilling or repair.

See issue #1806 for the performance problem this replaces: on a large,
heavily-crawled blog, the old `archives.js` loaded every entry and ran a
per-request `moment`/timezone grouping loop over all of them, which could
block the shared Node event loop long enough to crash the process.

---

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `index.js` | Public module surface. Re-exports `key`, `set`, `rebuild`, `months`, `bucket`, `isReady`. |
| `key.js` | Generates all Redis key strings used by the module. |
| `_bucket.js` | Shared helpers: computes an entry's `"YYYY-MM"` bucket from its `dateStamp` and the blog's timezone, the numeric sort score for a bucket, and the same "is this entry visible" rule `models/entry/_assign.js` uses for the `entries` list. |
| `set.js` | Keeps the index in sync for a single entry. Called alongside `models/tags`' `set()` from `models/entry/set.js`'s save queue. |
| `list.js` | Read-time queries: `months(blogID)`, `bucket(blogID, yearMonth)`, `isReady(blogID)`. |
| `rebuild.js` | Rebuilds the whole index for a blog from the canonical `entries` sorted set. |

### `tests/`

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `tests/set.js` | Incremental maintenance: adding/removing entries, moving between months on a `dateStamp` edit, refreshing score within the same month, pruning an emptied month, and timezone-aware bucketing. |
| `tests/rebuild.js` | Full rebuild: grouping, clearing stale buckets, setting the ready flag. |

---

## Redis Key Structure

Defined in `key.js`.

| Key pattern | Redis type | Contains |
|---|---|---|
| `blog:{blogID}:archives:{YYYY-MM}` | sorted set | Entry IDs published in that month, scored by `dateStamp` |
| `blog:{blogID}:archives:months` | sorted set | `"YYYY-MM"` strings for every month with at least one entry, scored by numeric `YYYYMM` |
| `blog:{blogID}:archives:entry:{entryID}` | string | The `"YYYY-MM"` bucket the entry currently belongs to |
| `blog:{blogID}:archives:ready` | string | Set once the index has been fully built for the blog |

---

## Public API

### `set(blogID, entry, timeZone, callback)`

Reconciles the archives index for a single entry.

- An entry is indexed only if it is visible the same way `models/entry/_assign.js` decides membership in the `entries` list (not a menu link, page, scheduled, deleted, or draft).
- Looks up the entry's current bucket from `blog:{blogID}:archives:entry:{entryID}` (not from a caller-supplied "previous" value - unlike tags, whose sorted-set key is stable, an archive bucket's key is derived from `dateStamp`, so this stored marker is the only reliable way to know which bucket to remove the entry from if it moves).
- If the entry moved to a different month (or became hidden), removes it from the old bucket; if still visible, adds/refreshes it in the new one.
- Prunes a month from `archives:months` once its last entry has moved out.

### `rebuild(blogID, callback)`

Rebuilds the whole index from scratch, from `models/entries`' `getAll` (already exactly the published/visible posts archives should show). Deletes existing buckets first (cheap - proportional to the number of distinct months, not entry count), then rewrites everything in one `multi`, then sets the ready flag. `callback(err, entryCount)`.

Called from:
- `app/sync/fix/archives-index.js`, on every blog sync, comparing the `entries` list count against the index (self-healing).
- `scripts/archives/backfill.js`, to warm every blog's index in one pass (e.g. right after deploying this module).
- `app/models/blog/set.js`, fire-and-forget, whenever a blog's `timeZone` changes - every existing bucket is keyed by year/month in the *old* timezone and would otherwise go stale.
- `app/blog/render/retrieve/archives.js`, synchronously, if a blog's index isn't ready yet at render time (belt-and-suspenders for a blog that hasn't synced or been backfilled).

### `months(blogID)` / `bucket(blogID, yearMonth)` / `isReady(blogID)`

Read-time queries used by `archives.js`. `months` returns `[{ yearMonth, count }]` newest first; `bucket` returns that month's entry IDs, newest first.
